+`plot-assisted-comparison.py` reads the existing analysis JSON without changing records or tests. Each Spearman coefficient correlates scheduled and adaptive participant averages for the same measure, using average ranks for ties rounded to twelve decimals. Scatterplot coordinates are not jittered; coincident pairs have larger markers. Eight measures cover completion, duration, overall workload, frustration and the four assistance ratings. `assisted-comparison.json` records the analysis hash and exact coefficients. Within-condition matrices remain an internal audit only and are no longer displayed.
